secubox-torrent (2.2.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Torrent is now a "sas" (staging area): downloads are CONSERVED BY DEFAULT —
    nothing auto-disappears anymore (fixes "yesterday's transfers vanished").
    Purge is OPT-IN: POST /api/v1/torrent/ephemeral/<ih> {seconds} marks a
    torrent to auto-delete after a delay; the sweep only ever deletes torrents
    whose opt-in purge time has passed (disk-floor safety valve reclaims marked-
    ephemeral only, never conserved content).
  * Library keep-by-default + ephemeral_until model (+ migration that flips
    legacy kept=0 rows to conserved, so an upgrade never purges existing data)
    + peertube_status/peertube_url columns for the coming PeerTube conserve.
  * resumeLibrary no longer re-adds every torrent to the engine on restart
    (that re-verified/re-hashed each file — the CPU storm that saturated the
    loop). The library keeps every conserved row; the engine loads a torrent
    LAZILY the first time it is streamed (Engine.ensureLoaded on /stream and
    /files). Restart-survival + no re-hash verified live on gk2.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Wed, 30 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0200

